BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:163358@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20260531T085128Z
DTSTART:20260514T160000Z
SUMMARY:Notice of Updates to Resource Fuel Mix Reporting
DESCRIPTION:ISO New England is updating the reporting of its generation resource mix with a new classification of fuel categories. Effective May 14\, 2026\, most electric storage facilities (e.g.\, batteries) will be reported as a standalone fuel category\, labeled as “Batteries.” Previously\, these resources were included in the “Other” category. Please note that Pumped Storage will continue to be categorized under the “Hydro” category.\n\nGiven the increasing number of electric storage facilities in the New England region\, this change provides additional detail about the resource mix. The update will be reflected across the various related reports and charts:\n\n\n	Web Services: Data returned via the /genfuelmix API endpoints will include the new data under this category. For a full list of categories\, please refer to the updated Fuel Category documentation.\n	CSV Reports: The new category will be included in the reports found within the Dispatch Fuel Mix reporting structure.\n	ISO Express: Both the Resource Mix Graph and Resource Mix Chart on the ISO Express dashboard will display the new category.\n	ISO to Go app: The Resource Mix Graph and related data in the mobile app will also be updated to reflect the new category.\n\n\nPlease note that while the format of the reports\, web services\, and data structures will not change\, participants will begin seeing these new values in the existing fields starting May 14. The change is prospective and will only affect the data as reported starting on May 14.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=163358
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=163358
END:VEVENT
